== ERL_LIBS=/usr/lib/elixir/lib
  lib_dir(elixir)="/usr/lib/elixir/lib/elixir"
  lib_dir(logger)="/usr/lib/elixir/lib/logger"
  lib_dir(mix)="/usr/lib/elixir/lib/mix"
  lib_dir(req)={error,bad_name}
  which('Elixir.Logger')="/usr/lib/elixir/lib/logger/ebin/Elixir.Logger.beam"
  which('Elixir.String')="/usr/lib/elixir/lib/elixir/ebin/Elixir.String.beam"
  which('Elixir.Req')=non_existing
== ERL_LIBS unset
  lib_dir(elixir)={error,bad_name}
  lib_dir(logger)={error,bad_name}
  lib_dir(mix)={error,bad_name}
  lib_dir(req)={error,bad_name}
  which('Elixir.Logger')=non_existing
  which('Elixir.String')=non_existing
  which('Elixir.Req')=non_existing
== wall time: erlc on a trivial module vs VM+check (VM start+halt is the floor for any Erlang tool; bsc is already a running VM)
  erlc t.erl: 232 ms
  erlc t.erl: 267 ms
  erlc t.erl: 230 ms
  erl -noshell -eval halt: 180 ms
  erl -noshell -eval halt: 165 ms
  erl -noshell -eval halt: 140 ms
  in-VM cost of check for 9 apps (lib_dir x9, mean of 1000 runs), microseconds:
  68.45 us per 9-app check
